# Vibe Coding Protocol — Cursor conventions sink
#
# Cursor reads this file on every Composer invocation. Drop the kit's full
# rules into .cursor/rules/ for topic-scoped advice (see README.md in this dir).
#
# Auto-detection: vibe-install picks this pack when it sees .cursor/ or .cursorrules
# in the cwd, or CURSOR_TRACE_ID / CURSOR_SESSION_ID in the env.

## Always

- Run lint + typecheck + tests before declaring done.
- Reject any new dep that isn't registry-verified (`npm view <name> version`) and license-audited.
- Document gotchas in `docs/gotchas.md` on discovery.
- Run `/vibe-verify` (mapped to Composer command) before claiming done on any user-visible feature.
- Update `CHANGELOG.md [Unreleased]` for user-visible changes.
- Write `docs/handoffs/<date>-<slug>.md` at session end (you do this manually — Cursor has no Stop hook).

## Never

- Edit committed migrations. → create a new one.
- Disable lint rules or bypass tests (`--no-verify`, `skip-ci`, `eslint-disable`) without justification.
- Hardcode secrets, tokens, URLs, environment-specific values.
- Use TypeScript `any` without justification.
- Commit `.env*` files.
- `rm -rf`, force-push, recursive deletes. → run `kit/bin/hooks/guard-unsafe.sh` first.

## Spec-first gate (run at every task start)

> **Planner is optional. Spec-first is not.**

Cursor is the implementation agent **and** the requirements-discovery agent when no applicable Spec exists. Run the gate at `kit/templates/spec-first-gate.md`:

1. Trivial change → proceed without a Spec.
2. Existing in-progress Spec → resume.
3. Awaiting-approval Spec → stop; the user must set `Status: in-progress`.
4. No applicable Spec, non-trivial work → enter DISCOVERY MODE (`prompts/00-anchor.md` § Discovery protocol). One question at a time. Then write `docs/requirements/<feature>/spec.md` with `Status: awaiting-approval` and **stop**. Do NOT implement in the same turn.
5. After approval, implement.

The user is the human-approval gate, not a paste-bridge.

## Two-role model (Planner optional)

- **Planner side** *(optional)*: any chat AI (Claude.ai, ChatGPT, Gemini) with `prompts/` files. No install.
- **Coder side**: Cursor reads `.cursor/rules/` + `.cursorrules` + `.cursor/commands/`. **If no applicable Spec exists, runs Discovery itself** (see spec-first gate above).
- **Verifier**: `kit/bin/vibe-verify` (run manually; not auto-fired).
- The Spec is the bridge between intent and code. The Planner is one way to produce it.

## Spec is the contract

- `docs/SPEC.md` — milestone-level.
- `docs/requirements/<feature>/spec.md` — feature-level contract.
- Each acceptance criterion = one test.
- When in doubt, the spec wins. Update the spec before changing the code, not after.

## Slash commands

The kit's `/vibe-*` commands work in Cursor (same `.md` format). Invoke in Composer:

- `/vibe-spec profile-photo-upload` — write feature spec
- `/vibe-verify` — AC↔test checker
- `/vibe-handoff` — write handoff doc
- `/vibe-ship` — CHANGELOG + handoff + ready-to-commit

## What Cursor doesn't auto-fire (vs Claude Code)

| Claude Code | Cursor |
|---|---|
| PostToolUse-on-Edit (format) | Composer has built-in formatter on save |
| PreToolUse-on-Bash (guard) | **No equivalent** — run `kit/bin/hooks/guard-unsafe.sh` manually |
| Stop-time handoff | **No equivalent** — call `/vibe-handoff` at session end |

You do the kill list manually. The rules in `.cursor/rules/` are advisory — Cursor reads them but doesn't *enforce*.

## When to switch to Claude Code

- Need destructive-pattern guard on Bash.
- Need Stop-time handoff automation.
- Need per-session memory persistence.

Or run both: Cursor for editing, Claude Code on `/vibe-review-pr` for a second pair of eyes.
